--- 1-3: a clean CV reaches the Talent Pool, whatever the profession ---
  PASS 1. clean construction CV goes straight to the Talent Pool as Core
  PASS 2. clean support-function CV is auto-ingested as Support
  PASS 3. an unrelated professional is auto-ingested, classified, NOT rejected

--- 4-6: no vacancy needed, and partial contact details are fine ---
  PASS 4. the pipeline does not depend on hiring requests existing
  PASS 5. name + phone, no email, is enough to auto-ingest
  PASS 6. name + email, no phone, is enough to auto-ingest

--- 7-10: duplicates, updates and lookalikes ---
  PASS 7. the identical CV twice produces ONE candidate
  PASS 8. an updated CV from an existing candidate keeps one person and records the document
  PASS 7. a namesake with different contacts becomes its OWN flagged candidate

--- uncertainty is LABELLED, not blocked ---
  PASS 2b. no email but a usable phone: Talent Pool, no Contact Missing flag
  PASS 2c. no contact at all: Talent Pool WITH Contact Missing
  PASS 4. sparse professional data: Talent Pool WITH Incomplete Profile
  PASS 5. low confidence on identity: Talent Pool WITH Low Confidence
  PASS 9. a completely unreadable file is a hard exception — no candidate
  PASS 10. no usable name is a hard exception — no candidate
  PASS 12. two CVs in one email are processed independently
  PASS 14. a candidate-record rule the reader got past keeps the CV

--- 15-18: idempotency, language, and the Application rule ---
  PASS 15. re-running the same ingest twice creates no second candidate
  PASS 16. an Arabic CV is ingested on its own merits
  PASS 17. a mixed Arabic/English CV classifies from the part it can read
  PASS 18. a clean auto-ingest creates NO Application
  PASS 18b. a CV uploaded against a requisition is never auto-ingested

--- classification, on its own ---
  PASS classification never returns something outside the five buckets
  PASS an empty profile is Unclassified, not a crash

--- classification is a search fact, never a review state ---
  PASS C1. an unclassifiable but clean CV still goes to the Talent Pool
  PASS C2. an Arabic-only CV is Unclassified and still auto-ingested
  PASS C3. no classification bucket carries review language
  PASS C4. the gate never reads the classification

--- an updated CV from someone already in the pool ---
  PASS U1. a newer CV refreshes career data, keeps one candidate and both documents
  PASS U2. identity and contact are never rewritten by an automatic refresh
  PASS U3. empty fields are filled from the newer CV
  PASS U4. a shared contact with a DIFFERENT person: separate flagged candidate, other record untouched
  PASS U5. a re-sent identical CV changes nothing and still needs nobody
  PASS U6. the refresh policy never lists an identity field as refreshable

--- flagged candidates are first-class members of the Talent Pool ---
  PASS 11. a flagged candidate is searchable by every ordinary field
  PASS 12. each label is its own Talent Pool filter
